window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-89d012f80d1d345a"]={"key":"ny_main-89d012f80d1d345a","group":"ny_main","uid":"89d012f80d1d345a","rank":68,"title":"underhill vantridge decision memo","occupation":"private_detectives_investigators","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are Alia Nightingale, the investigator responsible for closing Underhill Mutual’s Vantridge Manufacturing retail-counter case file this week. Lachlan Wolstenholme will use your memorandum to decide whether to authorize a targeted employee interview and an amended access-control arrangement, so the document needs to support an operational decision rather than merely repeat the contents of the exports. Work from the supplied `case_authority_and_scope.docx`, `counter_visit_evidence.xlsx`, `access_activity_extract.xlsx`, and `england_wales_requirements_snapshot.pdf`. The authority note sets out the case purpose, the source-visit key used across the evidence, the scope of the review, the changes you are authorized to record in the case file, and the operational deadline. The two workbooks contain the retail-counter and access activity material that must be reconciled; they are complete, but some evidence appears in overlapping rows, one workbook retains a helper column that is no longer authoritative and contains stale values, and a unit rate is represented with small floating-point differences between records. The England and Wales snapshot is the frozen requirements source for 12 May 2027, so do not browse for a newer rule or supplement it with an uncited internet source. Produce `vantridge_case_decision_memo.pdf` and write it into the top level of the working directory where you start, using exactly that filename. The memorandum should identify the case, the client, the investigator, the decision-maker, the relevant date and jurisdiction, and the question Lachlan must decide. It should give a clear recommendation on the targeted interview and the amended access controls, with the proposed owner, scope, timing, review or end point, and immediate next action concrete enough for a frontline employee to carry out. Keep the recommendation proportionate to what the supplied evidence actually establishes: distinguish observed records from interpretation, identify material uncertainty, and do not present a correlation or a near-equal rate as proof of misconduct. The evidence section needs to provide a usable reconciliation of the source material, with each retained evidential record traceable to its source and with the source-visit key used consistently. Duplicate or overlapping rows must not create a second incident, visit, rate, or access event in the decision basis. Explain how you treated the small rate differences and why the treatment is operationally defensible without implying more precision than the sources support. Do not use the retired helper column as evidence, a grouping key, or a reason for the recommendation; if you reproduce a reconciliation table, leave that retired convenience field out rather than copying its stale values. Apply the scope stated in the authority note, including any record that the source materials identify as outside the case question, and do not turn an out-of-scope item into a new allegation or control requirement. Set out the authorized case-file changes you recorded, including what was changed, what source or authority supported it, and what remains a recommendation for Lachlan rather than a completed system action. Do not claim that you altered the source workbooks or an external access-management system if the supplied material only authorizes a documented case-file update. The memorandum may use tables, but it must remain readable when printed, use selectable text, and include source references or clear provenance beside the factual findings. Preserve the distinction between the source facts, the reconciliation judgement, the legal or policy considerations in the supplied snapshot, and the recommended decision. Do not invent people, addresses, account identifiers, incidents, rates, permissions, or legal requirements that are not supported by the supplied files. Use the names and organisations as provided in the case materials, and make the deadline and ownership explicit rather than leaving Lachlan to infer them. Return only the PDF in the working directory at the exact top-level filename specified above.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/case_authority_and_scope.docx` — Authoritative case brief identifying the parties, decision question, scope, source-visit key, operational deadline, authorized case-file changes, and the distinction between completed updates and proposed actions.\n- `references/counter_visit_evidence.xlsx` — Primary retail-counter evidence export containing visit references, dates, observations, employee associations, source identifiers, unit rates, and a retired helper column with stale values.\n- `references/access_activity_extract.xlsx` — Access activity export containing records that overlap with some counter-visit evidence and records relevant to the proposed access-control decision.\n- `references/england_wales_requirements_snapshot.pdf` — Frozen, text-extractable snapshot of the England and Wales requirements applicable to the interview, evidence handling, proportionality, access control, authorization, and audit trail as of 12 May 2027.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `vantridge_case_decision_memo.pdf` — A professional decision memorandum for Lachlan Wolstenholme that reconciles the supplied case evidence, explains the treatment of duplicate keys, stale helper values, and floating-point rate noise, records authorized case-file changes, and gives an executable interview and access-control recommendation. (Write the file into the top level of the solver's starting working directory using exactly the specified filename. The PDF must contain selectable text, be readable when printed, preserve source provenance, distinguish facts from judgement, use only supported names and facts, and contain no unresolved spreadsheet error strings or invented case details.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/access_activity_extract.xlsx","bytes":6291,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/8059ca2644a72171ff3da93bc7a5583648a40608795bd1adf6e3071b1bcfcef1.xlsx","sha256":"8059ca2644a72171ff3da93bc7a5583648a40608795bd1adf6e3071b1bcfcef1","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Export","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Access activity extract"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Vantridge Manufacturing | access ledger extract received 12 May 2027"]},{"r":"3","cells":[]},{"r":"4","cells":["Source Visit Key","Access Record ID","Activity Date/Time","Access Area","Access Action","Employee Association","Access Result","Source System"]},{"r":"5","cells":["SVK-270504-ALB-01","AX-7712","46511.38497685185","Retail Counter Pricing workspace","Viewed rate card","Odile Chidozie","Granted","Access ledger"]},{"r":"6","cells":["SVK-270506-ALB-02","AX-7721","46513.65424768518","Retail Counter Pricing workspace","Downloaded quote register","Odile Chidozie","Granted","Access ledger"]},{"r":"7","cells":["SVK-270508-ALB-03","AX-7734","46515.41922453704","Retail Counter Pricing workspace","Viewed rate card","Odile Chidozie","Granted","Access ledger"]},{"r":"8","cells":["SVK-270509-ALB-04","AX-7740","46516.56055555555","Retail Counter Pricing workspace","Exported quote register","Odile Chidozie","Granted","Access ledger"]},{"r":"9","cells":["SVK-270510-ALB-05","AX-7756","46517.67494212963","Retail Counter Pricing workspace","Viewed rate card","Odile Chidozie","Granted","Access ledger"]},{"r":"10","cells":["SVK-270511-WH-04","AX-7769","46518.34586805556","Warehouse Receiving","Badge entry","Idris Lockhart","Granted","Access ledger"]},{"r":"11","cells":["SVK-270511-ALB-06","AX-7762","46518.46270833333","Retail Counter Pricing workspace","Downloaded replacement quote","Odile Chidozie","Granted","Access ledger"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/case_authority_and_scope.docx","bytes":39812,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/99eb8edd5bb13543127e95d7722f268c232113038cff5e35ae9d901b7a69c5c3.docx","sha256":"99eb8edd5bb13543127e95d7722f268c232113038cff5e35ae9d901b7a69c5c3","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Case authority and scope\nVantridge Manufacturing retail-counter review\nCase reference\nUM-VM-2705-17\nClient\nVantridge Manufacturing\nInvestigator\nAlia Nightingale - Investigator, Underhill Mutual\nDecision-maker\nLachlan Wolstenholme - Case Operations Manager, Underhill Mutual\nJurisdiction\nEngland and Wales\nRequirements as-of\n12 May 2027\nOperational deadline\n14 May 2027, 16:00 BST\nPurpose and decision question\nUnderhill Mutual is reviewing a Vantridge Manufacturing retail-counter case file. Lachlan Wolstenholme must decide whether to authorize a targeted interview of Odile Chidozie about the in-scope retail-counter and pricing-record activity, and whether to authorize an amended access-control arrangement for the Retail Counter Pricing workspace. The question is whether those proportionate next steps are supported by the recorded evidence and can be authorized under the England and Wales requirements snapshot dated 12 May 2027.\nScope boundary\nInclude retail-counter visits and directly linked access activity from 4 May through 11 May 2027 where the source-visit key links the records. Review only activity relevant to pricing or quote records and Odile Chidozie's assigned access. A matching visit key, rate, or timestamp is an indicator to clarify, not a finding of intent or misconduct.\nThe Warehouse Receiving badge record with Source Visit Key SVK-270511-WH-04, associated with Idris Lockhart, is outside this case question. Retain it in the source corpus for auditability, but do not use it as a basis for the interview or an access restriction. Lachlan Almeida is Vantridge Manufacturing's retail-counter supervisor and may be a factual contact; he is not the subject of the proposed interview.\nSource-visit key\nThe exact field label is \"Source Visit Key\". Its value identifies one underlying evidential visit across the counter and access exports. Matching values are one visit even when they appear in both workbooks; different values remain separate visits even when an employee, date, or rate appears similar.\nAuthority and permitted case-file changes\nAlia Nightingale may add a canonical evidence index keyed by Source Visit Key, retain the originating source record IDs, record the scope disposition, and document any reconciliation or normalization judgement. She may record the case status as decision pending and attach the resulting memorandum.\nThis authority permits documentation in the case file only. It does not permit editing either source workbook or changing an external access-management system. Any interview and any access amendment remain recommendations for Lachlan Wolstenholme to approve. Idris Lockhart is the Underhill Mutual access administrator who supplied the access extract and can implement a separately approved change; Lachlan Almeida remains the Vantridge operational contact.\nDeadline\nLachlan Wolstenholme must record the decision and the next owner by 14 May 2027, 16:00 BST. Any approved interview arrangement and access-control instruction should be issued from that recorded decision.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/counter_visit_evidence.xlsx","bytes":7820,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/73f774ea8692fa657d73e7a8f20f48e13aa18719a25e7bdeae04ee8dd8ac0c6d.xlsx","sha256":"73f774ea8692fa657d73e7a8f20f48e13aa18719a25e7bdeae04ee8dd8ac0c6d","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Export","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Retail counter evidence export"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Vantridge Manufacturing | received 12 May 2027 | source identifiers retained"]},{"r":"3","cells":[]},{"r":"4","cells":["Source Visit Key","Source Record ID","Visit Date","Counter / Channel","Observation","Employee Association","Unit Rate (GBP)","Currency","Retired Visit Group"]},{"r":"5","cells":["SVK-270504-ALB-01","CV-1048","46511","Albemarle retail counter","Quote prepared for Vantridge order; customer requested 12 units","Odile Chidozie","18.75","GBP","VISIT-01"]},{"r":"6","cells":["SVK-270506-ALB-02","CV-1052","46513","Albemarle retail counter","Quote amended after quantity query; rate card consulted","Odile Chidozie","18.75","GBP","VISIT-01"]},{"r":"7","cells":["SVK-270508-ALB-03","CV-1061","46515","Albemarle retail counter","Counter order note recorded; supervisor review requested","Odile Chidozie","18.75","GBP","VISIT-07"]},{"r":"8","cells":["SVK-270508-ALB-03","CV-1061-R","46515","Albemarle retail counter","Counter order note recorded; supervisor review requested","Odile Chidozie","18.7500000002","GBP","VISIT-07"]},{"r":"9","cells":["SVK-270509-ALB-04","CV-1068","46516","Albemarle retail counter","Follow-up quote printed for customer collection","Odile Chidozie","18.75","GBP","VISIT-07"]},{"r":"10","cells":["SVK-270510-ALB-05","CV-1074","46517","Albemarle retail counter","Return query logged and price correction checked","Odile Chidozie","19.2","GBP","VISIT-10"]},{"r":"11","cells":["SVK-270511-ALB-06","CV-1080","46518","Albemarle retail counter","Replacement quote issued; supervisor sign-off noted","Odile Chidozie","19.2","GBP","VISIT-10"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/england_wales_requirements_snapshot.pdf","bytes":4011,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/2bd693abe722e6ec1ad31f42a1c91184e5a5a67b4c56f103457fbd40c36ba22c.pdf","sha256":"2bd693abe722e6ec1ad31f42a1c91184e5a5a67b4c56f103457fbd40c36ba22c","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"UNDERHILL MUTUAL | GOVERNANCE SNAPSHOT                                                                                  Frozen 12 May 2027\n\n\n\n\n              England and Wales requirements snapshot\n Frozen operational reference for the Vantridge Manufacturing case file\n\n   Jurisdiction           England and Wales                            Effective reference date   12 May 2027\n\n   Use                    Workplace investigation and access-control   Status                     Snapshot for this case; do not supplement with\n                          decisions within a recorded case purpose                                a newer or uncited source\n\n\n 1. Purpose limitation and scope\n Use case information only for the documented purpose and within the recorded scope. A record that is unrelated to the\n question under review must remain outside the decision basis. It must not be promoted into a new allegation, interview\n subject, or access restriction without a separately recorded purpose and authority.\n\n 2. Evidence handling and auditability\n Preserve supplied source exports in their received form. A working index may link overlapping records, but it must retain\n the originating source identifier and explain the basis for de-duplication, normalization, or interpretation. Keep the scope\n decision and any material uncertainty in the case record so another reviewer can reproduce the decision basis.\n\n 3. Targeted workplace interviews\n An interview should be limited to the employee, issue, records, and period relevant to the documented question. The\n employee should have a fair opportunity to explain the recorded activity. Record the purpose, date, attendees, questions\n or topics, relevant source references, and outcome. Preliminary indicators, correlations, or access matches are not\n findings of misconduct on their own.\n\n 4. Access-control changes\n An amended access arrangement must be approved by the designated decision-maker before implementation. Specify\n the resource, permission, affected account or role, reason, implementation owner, and effective time. Use the\n least-privilege change that addresses the recorded operational need; do not apply a broader suspension without a\n separate rationale.\n\n 5. Review, expiry, and audit trail\n Every temporary access amendment must have a review or expiry point and a condition for restoration, revision, or\n continuation. The implementation record must identify who approved and implemented the change, what was changed,\n when it took effect, why it was needed, and when the review or end decision is due. The case file should link that record\n to the decision and the preserved source evidence.\n\n Application note\n This is a frozen operational snapshot for the named case and date. It is not a live legal update and does not replace\n case-specific legal advice or any separate internal approval process.\n\n\n\n\nEngland and Wales | Internal operational reference                                                                                   Page 1\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/vantridge_case_decision_memo.pdf","bytes":14749,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/4cc6302ebc1c4f0019054df3428c2c134ae0c3273b5109b5033ecb87681ead99.pdf","sha256":"4cc6302ebc1c4f0019054df3428c2c134ae0c3273b5109b5033ecb87681ead99","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"UNDERHILL MUTUAL | DECISION MEMORANDUM                                                                                      UM-VM-2705-17\n\n\n\n\n                                               Decision memorandum\n Vantridge Manufacturing retail-counter case file\n\n CASE                                                 CLIENT                                       INVESTIGATOR\n UM-VM-2705-17                                        Vantridge Manufacturing                      Alia Nightingale\n\n DECISION-MAKER                                       JURISDICTION / AS-OF                         DECISION DEADLINE\n Lachlan Wolstenholme                                 England and Wales / 12 May 2027              14 May 2027, 16:00 BST\n\n\n   DECISION REQUIRED                                                            RECOMMENDATION\n\n\n   Lachlan Wolstenholme must decide by 14 May 2027,                             Authorize the targeted interview. Approve in principle\n   16:00 BST whether to authorize a targeted interview of                       a temporary, least-privilege removal of\n   Odile Chidozie and an amended access-control                                 export/download rights for Odile Chidozie in the Retail\n   arrangement under the supplied England and Wales                             Counter Pricing workspace, retaining view-only\n   requirements snapshot.                                                       access. Neither action is completed by this\n                                                                                memorandum.\n\n 1. Case question and scope\n This memorandum answers the question in the authority note: are the recorded retail-counter and directly linked access\n records sufficient to justify a focused interview and a narrow access amendment, without treating a correlation or a\n near-equal rate as proof of misconduct? The answer is yes for those proportionate information-gathering and protective\n steps, subject to Lachlan's recorded approval. The evidence establishes recorded activity and an unresolved question about\n the purpose and handling of quote-register downloads; it does not establish intent or misconduct.\n Scope is limited to retail-counter pricing or quote activity from 4 to 11 May 2027 linked by the exact field label Source Visit\n Key. The source record with key SVK-270511-WH-04 (access record AX-7769 [X]) is a Warehouse Receiving badge event\n associated with Idris Lockhart and is outside the case question. It is retained for auditability but excluded from findings,\n interview scope, and controls. Lachlan Almeida is identified in the authority note as Vantridge Manufacturing's retail-counter\n supervisor and may be a factual contact; he is not the proposed interview subject.\n\n 2. Source facts and reconciliation\n Source facts. The counter export records the visit observations, employee association, source record IDs, dates, and unit\n rates. The access extract records the activity time, workspace, action, result, employee association, and access record IDs.\n Factual findings below are traceable to the row-level IDs shown in the tables. [C] = counter_visit_evidence.xlsx; [X] =\n access_activity_extract.xlsx; [A] = case_authority_and_scope.docx; [R] = england_wales_requirements_snapshot.pdf.\n Reconciliation judgement. I grouped rows only on the authority-defined Source Visit Key. A matching key is one\n underlying visit even when the row is present in both exports; a different key remains a separate visit. The counter export's\n Retired Visit Group helper field was not read as evidence, used as a grouping key, or copied into this decision basis. Its\n values conflict with the independent source keys (for example, separate keys are assigned the same legacy group), so\n relying on it would make the index non-reproducible.\n For rates, I used an absolute-difference tolerance of GBP 0.000001 for reconciliation only. Values within that tolerance are\n displayed to two decimal places; this avoids machine floating-point noise without claiming more precision than the source\n supports. The two representations for SVK-270508-ALB-03 are 18.7500000000 and 18.7500000002 GBP, so they are one\n operational rate for this index. The 18.75 and 19.20 values on distinct keys remain distinct; the tolerance does not erase that\n difference.\n\n\n\n\nInternal case file | Sources frozen for this review                                                                                Page 1\n\fUNDERHILL MUTUAL | DECISION MEMORANDUM                                                                                                               UM-VM-2705-17\n\n\n\n\n Canonical retained evidence basis (one row per distinct source key)\n Source Visit Key             Date          Employee                 Counter observation                          Counter source      Access            Rate used\n                                                                                                                  record              source record\n\n SVK-270504-ALB-01            04 May        Odile Chidozie           Albemarle retail counter: Quote prepared     CV-1048 (row 5)     AX-7712 (row 5)   18.75\n                              2027                                   for Vantridge order; customer requested 12\n                                                                     units\n\n SVK-270506-ALB-02            06 May        Odile Chidozie           Albemarle retail counter: Quote amended      CV-1052 (row 6)     AX-7721 (row 6)   18.75\n                              2027                                   after quantity query; rate card consulted\n\n SVK-270508-ALB-03            08 May        Odile Chidozie           Albemarle retail counter: Counter order      CV-1061 (row 7)     AX-7734 (row 7)   18.75\n                              2027                                   note recorded; supervisor review             CV-1061-R (row 8)\n                                                                     requested\n\n SVK-270509-ALB-04            09 May        Odile Chidozie           Albemarle retail counter: Follow-up quote    CV-1068 (row 9)     AX-7740 (row 8)   18.75\n                              2027                                   printed for customer collection\n\n SVK-270510-ALB-05            10 May        Odile Chidozie           Albemarle retail counter: Return query       CV-1074 (row 10)    AX-7756 (row 9)   19.20\n                              2027                                   logged and price correction checked\n\n SVK-270511-ALB-06            11 May        Odile Chidozie           Albemarle retail counter: Replacement        CV-1080 (row 11)    AX-7762 (row      19.20\n                              2027                                   quote issued; supervisor sign-off noted                          11)\n\n\n The index contains 6 in-scope canonical keys from 7 counter rows and 7 access rows. The repeated counter rows CV-1061 and CV-1061-R are\n lineage for the single key SVK-270508-ALB-03, not a second incident.\n\n 3. Chronology and what it supports\n The chronology below is a source-led sequence of access events linked to the same 6 in-scope keys. Each event shows a\n granted action in the Retail Counter Pricing workspace and is associated in the export with Odile Chidozie. That association\n supports a focused clarification interview. It does not, without Odile's explanation or further evidence, establish why a\n download or export occurred, who requested it, whether material was retained, or whether it was shared.\n When                       Source Visit Key                 Area / action                                                Employee                   Source ID\n\n 04 May 2027 09:14:22       SVK-270504-ALB-01                Retail Counter Pricing workspace                             Odile Chidozie             AX-7712\n                                                             Viewed rate card\n\n 06 May 2027 15:42:07       SVK-270506-ALB-02                Retail Counter Pricing workspace                             Odile Chidozie             AX-7721\n                                                             Downloaded quote register\n\n 08 May 2027 10:03:41       SVK-270508-ALB-03                Retail Counter Pricing workspace                             Odile Chidozie             AX-7734\n                                                             Viewed rate card\n\n 09 May 2027 13:27:12       SVK-270509-ALB-04                Retail Counter Pricing workspace                             Odile Chidozie             AX-7740\n                                                             Exported quote register\n\n 10 May 2027 16:11:55       SVK-270510-ALB-05                Retail Counter Pricing workspace                             Odile Chidozie             AX-7756\n                                                             Viewed rate card\n\n 11 May 2027 11:06:18       SVK-270511-ALB-06                Retail Counter Pricing workspace                             Odile Chidozie             AX-7762\n                                                             Downloaded replacement quote\n\n\n Requirements considered\n Requirement in supplied snapshot [R]                 Application here\n\n Purpose limitation and scope                         Keep the Warehouse Receiving record outside the decision; do not turn it into a new allegation or\n                                                      restriction.\n\n Targeted, fair interview                             Ask only about the linked visits and the recorded download/export actions, give Odile an opportunity to\n                                                      explain, and record the outcome.\n\n Least privilege and approval                         Limit the proposed change to export/download permission in the named workspace; Lachlan approves\n                                                      and Idris implements only after approval.\n\n Review, expiry, and audit trail                      Use the earlier of 21 May 2027 or completion of the interview/evidence review as the review point; log\n                                                      approver, implementer, scope, reason, time, and end/revision decision.\n\n Evidence integrity                                   Preserve both source exports, cite source IDs, and retain the key-based reconciliation and rate\n                                                      tolerance in the case file.\n\n\n\n\nInternal case file | Sources frozen for this review                                                                                                             Page 2\n\fUNDERHILL MUTUAL | DECISION MEMORANDUM                                                                                                    UM-VM-2705-17\n\n\n\n\n 4. Action recommendation\n Decision item               Recommendation                                                        Owner / timing / endpoint\n\n Targeted interview          Authorize a focused interview of Odile Chidozie about the             Owner: Alia Nightingale to arrange and conduct.\n                             retail-counter visits and the granted download/export actions for     When: complete by 14 May 2027, 16:00 BST.\n                             SVK-270506-ALB-02, SVK-270509-ALB-04, SVK-270511-ALB-06.              End point: record questions, Odile's explanation,\n                             The interview is for clarification, not a finding of misconduct.      attendees, date, and outcome in the case file; close or\n                                                                                                   revise the recommendation after that record is\n                                                                                                   reviewed.\n\n Access amendment            Authorize in principle a temporary least-privilege change for Odile   Owner: Idris Lockhart, access administrator, after\n                             Chidozie: retain view-only access to the Retail Counter Pricing       Lachlan's recorded approval.\n                             workspace, remove export/download permission, and leave other         Review: 21 May 2027 or completion of the targeted\n                             access untouched. This addresses the specific recorded actions        interview and evidence review, whichever is earlier.\n                             while avoiding a blanket suspension.                                  End/revise: Lachlan records whether\n                                                                                                   export/download remains needed; restore or narrow\n                                                                                                   the change accordingly.\n\n\n Immediate next action for Lachlan: by 14 May 2027, 16:00 BST, record approve or decline for each decision item in the\n case file and name the owner. If approved, Alia Nightingale sends Odile Chidozie a focused interview invitation and Idris\n Lockhart receives the specific view-only/export-download instruction. No instruction should be treated as executed until the\n responsible owner records the action and its audit details.\n Why this is proportionate. The proposed interview addresses an identifiable information gap in the access chronology.\n The proposed access amendment protects the named pricing workspace while preserving the view access needed for the\n counter role. The recommendation does not rely on the excluded Idris Lockhart record, the retired helper values, or rate\n similarity as evidence of wrongdoing.\n\n\n\n\nInternal case file | Sources frozen for this review                                                                                                 Page 3\n\fUNDERHILL MUTUAL | DECISION MEMORANDUM                                                                                                              UM-VM-2705-17\n\n\n\n\n 5. Authorized case-file changes recorded\n I recorded the following changes within the case file under the authority note. These entries document the evidence and\n decision status; they do not alter the source workbooks or an external access-management system.\n Recorded case-file change                                       Support                                                    Status / boundary\n\n Added a canonical evidence index keyed by Source Visit          case_authority_and_scope.docx, Authority and permitted     Completed in this case-file\n Key, with one retained representation per key, counter          case-file changes; counter_visit_evidence.xlsx;            memorandum. Source workbooks\n and access source IDs, and the scope disposition for            access_activity_extract.xlsx                               were not edited.\n SVK-270511-WH-04.\n\n Recorded the reconciliation note: same-key rows are             case_authority_and_scope.docx, Source-visit key;           Completed as an analyst\n linked; the Retired Visit Group field is excluded; the two      counter_visit_evidence.xlsx source records CV-1061 and     judgement. The tolerance is for\n near-equal rate representations for SVK-270508-ALB-03           CV-1061-R                                                  reconciliation only and does not\n are operationally normalized to GBP 18.75 for this                                                                         assert commercial identity.\n decision.\n\n Updated the case-file status to decision pending and            case_authority_and_scope.docx, Authority and permitted     Completed in the case file. The\n attached this memorandum for Lachlan Wolstenholme's             case-file changes                                          interview and access amendment\n decision.                                                                                                                  remain proposed actions, not\n                                                                                                                            completed system actions.\n\n\n\n Source register\n Reference                                                    Use in this memorandum\n\n case_authority_and_scope.docx [A]                            Case roles, question, scope boundary, exact Source Visit Key definition, authority, and deadline.\n\n counter_visit_evidence.xlsx [C]                              Visit dates, observations, employee association, source IDs, and unit-rate representations; row\n                                                              numbers are retained in the evidence index.\n\n access_activity_extract.xlsx [X]                             Access chronology, workspace, action, result, employee association, and access source IDs.\n\n england_wales_requirements_snapshot.pdf [R]                  Frozen England and Wales requirements as of 12 May 2027: purpose limitation, evidence\n                                                              handling, targeted interviews, authorization, least privilege, review/expiry, and audit trail.\n\n\n Prepared by Alia Nightingale, Investigator, Underhill Mutual. Status: decision pending. This memorandum records the analyst's reconciliation and\n recommendation for Lachlan Wolstenholme; it is not a finding of misconduct and is not evidence that an external access change has been executed.\n\n\n\n\nInternal case file | Sources frozen for this review                                                                                                            Page 4\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered artifact is a PDF memorandum with the exact requested filename.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted file name and file type.","grader_hint":"Check the top-level output filename and confirm that it opens as a PDF. This is a scaffolding item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF contains selectable, text-extractable content rather than being only a raster image.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Text extraction from the submitted PDF.","grader_hint":"Extract text from multiple pages or the full document and confirm that substantial memorandum text is available."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly identifies Underhill Mutual, Vantridge Manufacturing, Alia Nightingale, and Lachlan Wolstenholme in their supported roles.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case heading, opening statement, and role descriptions.","grader_hint":"Compare names and roles with the authority note; do not award for merely listing names with no role or case connection."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stated decision question, jurisdiction, and as-of date agree with the authority note and requirements snapshot.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision framing and jurisdiction/date references in the memorandum.","grader_hint":"Check that the memo concerns authorization of the targeted interview and amended access controls under the supplied England and Wales requirements as of the supplied date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The factual portions of the memorandum are traceable to the supplied case authority, counter-visit workbook, access-activity workbook, or requirements snapshot.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source list, citations, footnotes, table references, or equivalent provenance.","grader_hint":"Walk factual claims back to the four references. Credit clear provenance even if the memo uses a compact source key rather than formal footnotes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo states the source-visit key exactly as defined in the authority note and uses that key consistently in its reconciliation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method or reconciliation explanation and retained-record table.","grader_hint":"Compare the key's field name and meaning with the authority document; a different invented key does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The retained evidence basis contains one canonical representation for each distinct source-visit key, with duplicate rows not counted as separate visits or incidents.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reconciliation table, evidence index, or equivalent canonical record list.","grader_hint":"Derive the distinct-key set from the two workbooks and compare it with the memo's retained set; do not require a particular table layout."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Overlapping rows from the two workbooks are linked to the same underlying source visit where their stated key agrees, while genuinely separate keys remain separate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-source reconciliation and lineage references.","grader_hint":"Check both directions: same-key overlaps are not split into separate events, and different-key records are not collapsed merely because their employee or rate is similar."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each retained evidential record has enough source identification for another reviewer to locate its originating workbook record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source IDs, row labels, visit references, or equivalent locators in the memo.","grader_hint":"A generic statement that the workbooks were reviewed is insufficient; inspect whether retained records can actually be located."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo distinguishes source evidence from the reconciliation judgement used to select a canonical representation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Separate factual and method or judgement language.","grader_hint":"Credit wording that makes clear what the exports show and what Alia inferred or normalized, rather than presenting the normalization as a source fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The retired helper column is explicitly treated as non-authoritative and is omitted from the evidential basis, or is visibly marked as not used without reproducing its stale values.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reconciliation method and any reproduced evidence table.","grader_hint":"Compare the memo's grouping, inclusion, and conclusion against the authoritative key and source fields, not the helper values. The helper must not be used as a substitute for evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The explanation of why the retired helper was disregarded is clear enough that another investigator could understand the control weakness and reproduce the decision.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method note or evidence-quality discussion.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit connection between the helper's retired or stale status and the decision to rely on source-visit keys and source records instead."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo states a defensible rate-tolerance or normalization convention for the floating-point representations and applies it consistently.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rate reconciliation note and displayed rate values.","grader_hint":"The convention must be visible and used consistently; do not require a particular tolerance value, but reject silent equality or inconsistent treatment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The near-equal unit-rate representations that differ only by floating-point noise are treated as the same operational rate when they refer to the same source visit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rate comparison in the reconciliation.","grader_hint":"Compare the memo's treatment with the noisy duplicate representations in the references. Credit a normalized or clearly equivalent presentation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not use the tolerance to erase a genuinely different unit rate or to assert more precision than the source records support.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rate table and caveat surrounding rate interpretation.","grader_hint":"Check any legitimately different source rate remains distinguishable and that the memo does not describe floating-point equivalence as proof that the underlying business events were identical."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The material counter-visit observations, dates, employee associations, and source identifiers in the memo faithfully match the counter-visit workbook after reconciliation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence summary and retained-record table.","grader_hint":"Spot-check every retained key against the workbook; ignore harmless formatting changes but not changed facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The material access-activity facts and chronology in the memo faithfully match the access-activity workbook after overlapping records are resolved.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Access chronology and source references.","grader_hint":"Check timestamps or dates, access context, employee association, and source identifiers against the access workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo presents a coherent chronology in which dates and sequence relationships agree across both workbooks.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline or chronological narrative.","grader_hint":"Reconstruct the sequence from the source records and verify that the memo has not reordered or duplicated events in a way that changes meaning."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo attributes activity to an employee only where the supplied records support that association and distinguishes direct attribution from inference.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Employee references and qualification language.","grader_hint":"Compare each named employee finding with the source fields and look for appropriate uncertainty where the evidence is indirect."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo applies the case scope from the authority note and keeps records identified there as outside the decision question out of the recommendation basis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope statement and evidence selection.","grader_hint":"Check inclusion and exclusion against the authority note; do not require a particular label for excluded material if the boundary is clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The legal or policy considerations used in the recommendation are supported by, and accurately represented from, the supplied England and Wales requirements snapshot.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Requirements discussion and source attribution.","grader_hint":"Compare each cited requirement with the snapshot and reject uncited invented obligations or claims of current law beyond the frozen source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum gives Lachlan a clear decision recommendation rather than leaving the conclusion implicit in the evidence summary.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Executive conclusion or decision section.","grader_hint":"A reviewer should be able to answer what Lachlan should authorize, decline, or defer without interpreting the whole document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposed interview is targeted to the supported employee, issue, and evidence boundary in the source materials.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Interview recommendation.","grader_hint":"Compare the subject and purpose with the authority note and reconciled evidence; broad or unrelated interviews do not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The interview recommendation is proportionate and explains why an interview is warranted without asserting that the evidence already proves misconduct.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation rationale and uncertainty language.","grader_hint":"Credit a balanced explanation that connects the evidence to information still needed and avoids an overconfident accusation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum names a responsible owner for arranging or conducting the targeted interview and identifies the immediate next action.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action plan or recommendation table.","grader_hint":"The owner and action must be explicit enough for a frontline employee to execute, and must agree with the authority materials."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The interview recommendation includes the operational deadline from the authority note or an unambiguous action date tied to that deadline.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action deadline in the memo.","grader_hint":"Check against the supplied authority note; vague wording such as 'soon' or 'this week' without the stated operational anchor is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The access-control recommendation identifies the supported privilege or access area to be amended and does not recommend a generic, unexplained restriction.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Access-control recommendation.","grader_hint":"Compare the proposed change with the access records, authority note, and requirements snapshot."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposed access amendment is least-privilege and proportionate to the reconciled evidence and the supplied requirements.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Control design and rationale.","grader_hint":"Look for a focused limitation rather than an unnecessarily broad suspension or restriction, and require an evidence-based explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The access recommendation states an owner, a duration or review point, and the condition or action for ending or revising the amendment.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Implementation or control-action details.","grader_hint":"All three elements must be actionable; a control with no review or end mechanism is incomplete."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposed access change includes the required approval and audit-trail or logging treatment described in the requirements snapshot.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Control governance language.","grader_hint":"Check that approval and recordkeeping are addressed as applicable requirements, not merely implied by the word 'authorize'."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum records each authorized case-file change from the authority note, including what was changed, the supporting authority or source, and whether the action is completed or still proposed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case-file change record or equivalent section.","grader_hint":"Compare the memo's change record with the authorized-action language in the case authority document and check the completed-versus-proposed distinction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo does not claim that the supplied source workbooks or an external access-management system were altered when the sources only support a documented case-file update.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change-status language and limitations.","grader_hint":"Reject unsupported claims of system execution; credit precise language that limits the completed action to the authority granted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Names, dates, source-visit references, rate treatment, evidence conclusions, and recommended actions agree with one another throughout the memorandum.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-check of tables, narrative, conclusion, and action plan.","grader_hint":"Look for contradictions such as a person appearing in the timeline but not the recommendation, or a rate being described differently in the evidence and conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum is professionally usable by Lachlan and a frontline recipient: the decision, evidence basis, uncertainty, owner, deadline, and next actions can be found without reconstructing the analyst's reasoning.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered PDF as a whole.","grader_hint":"Judge navigation, hierarchy, readable tables, concise explanations, and whether the artifact supports the named next decision. Technical correctness alone is not enough."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo contains no spreadsheet error strings such as #REF!, #DIV/0!, or #VALUE! and does not carry stale helper values into the decision basis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Extracted PDF text and reproduced tables.","grader_hint":"Search the full extracted text and inspect any evidence tables for the listed error strings or copied helper values."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memo turns an out-of-scope record into a new allegation, interview subject, or access restriction, or recommends a broader unsupported access action than the supplied authority and evidence justify.","weight":-5.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope treatment, findings, and recommendation.","grader_hint":"Apply once for the over-production problem: identify whether an excluded item or unsupported restriction has been promoted into the decision. Do not also penalize the same fact under a separate credit item."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Alia Nightingale is an investigator at Underhill Mutual preparing a retail-counter case file concerning Vantridge Manufacturing. Lachlan Wolstenholme needs a concise decision memorandum that can support an authorized interview and access-control decision under the England and Wales requirements recorded for the relevant date.","difficulty_sources":["Reconciling overlapping evidence rows without counting the same source visit twice","Separating evidential records from a retired helper column containing stale values","Choosing and disclosing a defensible tolerance for floating-point noise in unit rates","Turning a reconciled evidence record into a proportionate, executable recommendation"],"authoring_plan":{"source_semantics":{"case_authority_and_scope":["Create a text-extractable case authority note for Underhill Mutual and Vantridge Manufacturing naming Alia Nightingale as investigator and Lachlan Wolstenholme as decision-maker.","State the decision question concerning a targeted interview and an amended access-control arrangement, the England and Wales jurisdiction, the as-of date, the case scope, and an operational deadline selected by the build agent.","Define the source-visit key by its exact field label and meaning across both workbooks. The key must identify one underlying evidential visit even when that visit appears in more than one export.","Record the authorized case-file changes Alia may document, including the evidence-index or case-status update and the distinction between documenting that update and merely recommending an external access-system action.","Identify the supported employee and the relevant operational issue using the permitted names, including Odile Chidozie where appropriate, and identify Idris Lockhart and Lachlan Almeida only in roles supported by the authority materials."],"counter_visit_evidence":["Create a complete text-extractable workbook of retail-counter evidence with the authority-defined source-visit key, source record identifiers, dates, observations, employee associations, and unit-rate fields.","Include overlapping records whose source-visit key matches records in the access-activity workbook. Include at least one same-visit rate representation differing only in floating-point precision and at least one legitimately different rate across distinct visits.","Include a clearly labelled retired helper column with stale values that would mislead a naive grouping or confidence assessment. The authoritative source fields must independently determine the correct reconciliation.","Keep all ordinary evidence fields populated and internally consistent; do not introduce missing-value, formula-error, malformed-date, contradictory-identity, or unrelated layout defects."],"access_activity_extract":["Create a complete text-extractable workbook of access events and related evidence with the same source-visit key, source identifiers, dates or times, access context, and employee associations.","Overlap selected records with the counter-visit workbook by the shared key, while retaining separate legitimate records with different keys.","Include a scope-designated record that is a real, internally consistent source row but is outside the case question according to the authority note; it must be tempting to include but should not support the final recommendation.","Provide enough supported chronology and access detail for a proportionate least-privilege recommendation, without requiring unsupported assumptions about intent or misconduct."],"england_wales_requirements_snapshot":["Create a frozen, text-extractable requirements snapshot explicitly dated 12 May 2027 for England and Wales.","Include requirements relevant to purpose limitation, proportionality, targeted interviewing, authorization, least-privilege access changes, review or expiry, and audit-trail recordkeeping.","Make the snapshot a plausible governing workplace artifact rather than a purpose-built answer key. It must support the recommendation but must not resolve the investigator's choice of rate tolerance or dictate the wording of the memorandum."]},"seeded_defects":["Duplicate or overlapping evidence rows across the supplied workbooks that must be reconciled using the source-visit key defined in the authority note.","A retired helper column in the counter-visit workbook whose stale values conflict with the authoritative source fields and must not be used or copied as evidence.","Floating-point noise in one unit-rate representation so exact machine equality fails even though the same operational rate is represented."],"transformation":["The solver reshapes the supplied case materials into one decision memorandum, retaining traceable canonical evidence rather than reproducing every source row.","The solver chooses and discloses a defensible rate tolerance, separates source facts from judgement, applies the supplied scope, and translates the requirements snapshot into an executable recommendation.","The solver documents the authorized case-file changes and clearly labels any interview or access-control action that remains a recommendation rather than a completed external system change."],"gold_derivation":{"canonical_records":"Derive the canonical evidential set by grouping all workbook records on the authority-defined source-visit key, checking that same-key overlaps represent the same underlying visit, and retaining source lineage for every canonical record.","rate_evaluation":"Identify the intentionally noisy same-visit unit-rate representations and verify that a professionally disclosed tolerance can classify them as operationally equivalent without collapsing the legitimately different rate on a separate key.","scope_evaluation":"Mark the authority-designated out-of-scope record as excluded from the findings and recommendation while retaining it in the source corpus for auditability.","recommendation_evaluation":"Use the supplied evidence relationships and requirements snapshot to support a targeted interview of the supported employee and a proportionate, least-privilege access amendment with an owner, deadline, review or end point, approval, and audit trail. The reference solution should express uncertainty and should not assert misconduct as established fact.","change_record_evaluation":"Compare the memorandum's documented case-file changes with the authorized actions in the case authority note and verify that completed case-file documentation is not represented as an external access-system change."},"quality_constraints":["All graded facts must be visible in text-extractable reference files.","Do not include any additional standard defects such as missing values, zero denominators, broken formulas, error tokens, conflicting source identities, or hidden image-only content.","Do not dictate sheet counts, row counts, column order, page layout, styling, or literal gold values; the build agent chooses those details.","The intentionally excluded scope record and omitted retired helper field are control-boundary conditions, not additional data-quality defects."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"case_authority_scope","filename":"case_authority_and_scope.docx","purpose":"Authoritative case brief identifying the parties, decision question, scope, source-visit key, operational deadline, authorized case-file changes, and the distinction between completed updates and proposed actions.","required":true,"discovery":"Open this supplied case note to establish the case context, the named key, the authorized action, and the deadline before relying on the workbook records."},{"artifact_id":"counter_visit_evidence","filename":"counter_visit_evidence.xlsx","purpose":"Primary retail-counter evidence export containing visit references, dates, observations, employee associations, source identifiers, unit rates, and a retired helper column with stale values.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this workbook as one of the evidence sources and inspect its field notes and source identifiers; the retired helper is not an authoritative evidence field."},{"artifact_id":"access_activity_extract","filename":"access_activity_extract.xlsx","purpose":"Access activity export containing records that overlap with some counter-visit evidence and records relevant to the proposed access-control decision.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this workbook together with the counter evidence to reconcile the source-visit records and establish the supported access chronology."},{"artifact_id":"ew_requirements_snapshot","filename":"england_wales_requirements_snapshot.pdf","purpose":"Frozen, text-extractable snapshot of the England and Wales requirements applicable to the interview, evidence handling, proportionality, access control, authorization, and audit trail as of 12 May 2027.","required":true,"discovery":"Consult this supplied snapshot for the jurisdictional requirements and cite or clearly attribute any requirement used in the recommendation."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"decision_memo","filename":"vantridge_case_decision_memo.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"A professional decision memorandum for Lachlan Wolstenholme that reconciles the supplied case evidence, explains the treatment of duplicate keys, stale helper values, and floating-point rate noise, records authorized case-file changes, and gives an executable interview and access-control recommendation.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file into the top level of the solver's starting working directory using exactly the specified filename. The PDF must contain selectable text, be readable when printed, preserve source provenance, distinguish facts from judgement, use only supported names and facts, and contain no unresolved spreadsheet error strings or invented case details."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"private_detectives_investigators","sector":"retail_trade","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":3.75,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Build the reference files from the semantic source specification, derive the canonical source-visit set and factual gold from those files, and have an independent reviewer walk the rendered reference memorandum against every rubric predicate. The reviewer should judge proportionality and usability using only the supplied requirements snapshot and case materials.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["The legal requirements are frozen in the supplied snapshot and are not independently validated against live sources.","The precise visual layout of the memorandum is intentionally left to the document author; grading focuses on readable execution and content relationships."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:28:45+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:28:45+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:28:45+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:28:45+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/89d012f80d1d345a","declared_deliverables":["vantridge_case_decision_memo.pdf"]};
